<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Compliance and eligibility</h1>
    <p>Who may order from this catalogue, and what the shop checks before anything is released.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <% if (jurisdictionPending) { %>
      <div class="note note-pending">
        <h3>Jurisdiction not confirmed</h3>
        <p>
          The country and state this business is licensed in have not been recorded in the site
          configuration yet. Until they are, the ages and rules below are shown as the common baseline for a
          licensed dealer in the United States and must not be relied on. They are replaced with the rules
          that actually apply once the licence holder confirms the jurisdiction.
        </p>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>
      Handguns and handgun frames listed here may be transferred only to a buyer aged
      <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeHandgun %> or over. Parts and accessories may be transferred only to a
      buyer aged <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeAccessory %> or over. You are asked to confirm your age before an
      order request can be submitted, and the shop verifies it with photographic identification before
      anything is released.
    </p>

    <h2>Prohibited persons</h2>
    <p>
      A person barred from possessing a firearm cannot buy one here. That includes anyone subject to a
      disqualifying conviction, a court order, or a restriction recorded against them by the relevant
      authority. Submitting an order request while prohibited is a criminal offence in most jurisdictions.
    </p>

    <h2>Local law varies</h2>
    <p>
      Magazine capacity limits, permitted models, roster requirements, waiting periods and permit
      requirements differ between states and between countries. An item appearing in this catalogue is not a
      statement that it is legal where you live. Checking your local rules is your responsibility, and the
      shop refuses any order it cannot lawfully complete.
    </p>

    <h2>How the shop verifies</h2>
    <% if (transferConfirmed) { %>
      <p><%= business.policy.transferProcessText %></p>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="note note-pending">
        <h3>Verification steps pending publication</h3>
        <p>
          The exact identification, background check and licence checks this dealer performs are supplied by
          the licence holder. They are not invented by the developer and they are not published here until
          the licence holder signs off the wording. Until then the shop confirms the steps with you directly
          before any item is released.
        </p>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <h2>Destinations the shop will not ship to</h2>
    <% if (restricted.length) { %>
      <ul><% restricted.forEach(function (d) { %><li><%= d %></li><% }); %></ul>
    <% } else { %>
      <p class="meta-updated">
        The restricted destination list has not been supplied yet. It is published here as a plain list once
        the licence holder provides it.
      </p>
    <% } %>

    <h2>Export</h2>
    <p>
      Firearms and many firearm parts are export controlled. Nothing in this catalogue is offered for export
      unless the shop states so in writing for that specific order, with the licences that permit it.
    </p>

    <h2>This is not legal advice</h2>
    <p>
      The pages on this site describe how the shop operates. They are not legal advice about your own
      position. If you are unsure whether you may lawfully buy or possess an item, speak to a lawyer or to
      the relevant authority before you order.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe a listing on this site is inaccurate or should not be offered in your jurisdiction,
      tell the shop through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and it will be reviewed.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
